{"name":"Persian Fable","hex":"#d4ebdd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fictitious narrative intended to enforce some useful truth or precept, usually with animals, etc. as characters; an apologue. Prototypically, Aesop's Fables.","Any story told to excite wonder; common talk; the theme of talk."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To compose fables; hence, to write or speak fiction; to write or utter what is not true.","To make up; to devise, and speak of, as true or real; to tell of falsely; to recount in the form of a fable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fable"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fable","blocks":[{"text":"Fable is a literary genre defined as a succinct fictional story, in prose or verse, that features animals, legendary creatures, plants, inanimate objects, or forces of nature that are anthropomorphised, and that illustrates or leads to a particular moral lesson, which may at the end be added explicitly as a concise maxim or saying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Cat_guarding_geese_c1120_BC_Egypt.jpg/330px-Cat_guarding_geese_c1120_BC_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fable","wikidata":"Q693"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg/500px-Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg/1280px-Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg/500px-Fabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Printed image of the fable of the blacksmith and the dog from the sixteenth century[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFabel_van_de_smid_en_de_hond.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABooks_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png"}],"sounds":{"fable":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/En-us-fable.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0c/En-us-fable.ogg/En-us-fable.ogg.mp3"}]}}}